= Rejected metadata representation
#text(size: 8pt, fill: rgb("#79542b"), weight: "bold")[Native instruction and allocation measurements · run-20261012T0543Z]

#image("rejected-memory.svg", width: 100%)

The second implementation recorded 5.51% fewer F4 instructions and 11.03% fewer F5 instructions, but failed the memory gate. The high-bit fallback's additional peak grew from 54,104 to 54,112 bytes across all primary and paired calls. The native probe measured the original index metadata at 48 bytes, the flat three-way enum at 56 bytes, and a nested representation at 48 bytes. The heap-resident column layout accounts for the observed eight-byte increase. METADATA-FIX explicitly extended the two-attempt stop rule by one bounded correction and rerun. It preserved inputs and gates, added a metadata-size regression assertion and retained all failed results. The superseded full-library run was interrupted, not counted as passed.

